    "fullDescription": "Analyst: Healthcare, EHR, BI, SQL Report Development Troubleshoot CPT Start date :10/26/2026 End Date :10/25/2027 Submission deadline : 10/21/2026 Client Info : NCDIT-HIEA Note: *Remote *Webcam Interview Only *This is a hybrid/remote position; preference will be given to applicants residing in North Carolina. Description: Able to work successfully with guidance; cannot provide leadership to others; able to manage simple to medium complexity work efforts. This position supports the HIE Medicaid Services (HMS) program, a collaboration between NC HIEA and the NC Department of Health and Human Services (NCDHHS) Division of Health Benefits (DHB), also known as NC Medicaid. Part of this program focuses on enhancing Medicaid quality and population health efforts through improved data exchange, focusing on: 1. Transitioning to digital quality measures (dQMs), 2. Improving health-related social needs (HRSN) data exchange, and 3. Enhancing care management data sharing. The HMS Analyst will support the implementation, expansion, and ongoing operations of Medicaid data exchange services within NC HIEA, with a strong focus on improving HRSN data capture and onboarding early adopters. This role is responsible for translating program and partner needs into clear technical and workflow requirements, supporting Continuity of Care Document (CCD) / Admission-Discharge-Transfer (ADT) data integration efforts, and coordinating cross-team activities to enhance data quality and interoperability. The analyst will work closely with internal teams and external stakeholders to troubleshoot issues, guide testing and onboarding, and ensure that new data connections are implemented accurately, securely, and in alignment with statewide population health priorities. The position requires strong analytical skills, deep familiarity with health information exchange standards, and the ability to communicate effectively with both technical and non-technical partners.",
