    "description": "Consultant: Architecting, Government Experience, AEM, Java Development Agile Start date : 11/17/2026 End Date : 12 Months from projected start date Submission deadline : 10/20/2026 5:00:00 PM Client Info : SCDOR Note: *Interview Process: 1 Round of Onsite Interviews *Work Location: Fully Onsite *Candidate location: Candidate must be a CURRENT SC resident. No relocation allowed. Description: The SC Dept. of Revenue is among the most sought-after agency in the state sector for contractors due to our reputation for accomplishing highly complex technology in a multi-layer secured environment. We are known for requiring skilled and professional workers that can get the job done well and on time. Our team is creative and hardworking. The DOR technology division implements technology using effective methodology and procedures, and we appreciate the insights and best practices that contractors bring with them. Company Culture: A strong and healthy organizational culture will drive our efforts and lead to success for all stakeholders. SCDOR strives to exemplify a culture that embodies: • Excellence demonstrated by focusing on proactive customer service. • Open Communication demonstrated through vibrant two-way communication with stakeholders. • Functional Security demonstrated through the protection of taxpayer information. • Leadership demonstrated by modeling integrity, ethical behavior, and the highest standards of conduct. • Visionary and Innovative planning and problem solving. • Ownership of problems by taking responsibility for actions and performance. • Accountability demonstrated through performance metrics and evaluations. • Collaboration among teams for everyday process improvement. • Empowering Employees to make a positive difference by enhancing their skills and knowledge, as well as recognizing their contributions. • Professionalism demonstrated by competent, resourceful, accountable, and courteous employees. Why is this position open? This is a 3-year reposting for an existing contractor position. The incumbent contractor is likely to reapply. Scope of the project: DOR has implemented Adobe Experience Manager (AEM), and Power Business Intelligence (PBI) as its tool set for forms, workflow and Dashboard/Report development. DOR wishes to engage a systems software programmer experienced in AEM, PBI and Data Architecture. The following description details the skills and tasks that are required of the systems software programmer. Under limited supervision, the contractor will serve as a systems software programmer reporting directly to a functional manager. Contractor will be a team member that ensures the stability and integrity of data, and server services through monitoring, maintenance, support, and optimization of all server infrastructure. This individual has 24/7 on-call responsibilities shared with the group. KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Works with consultants, application developers and end users to develop the logical data model and data architecture of assigned application. Designs relational databases within the architectural framework to meet application needs. Serves as lead database designer for assigned application systems. Develops and implements standards for database design. Writes and maintains stored procedures as needed; develops standards for the use of stored procedures, object relational mappers, and other means of database access. Develops standards for application handling of databases, including error handling. Builds database utilities as needed for application use, such as SQL Server Integration Services (SSIS) packages and database scripts. Analyzes anticipated data volumes and patterns of use; gains knowledge of agency data usage to improve efficiency of database access and m",
