    "description": "Manager: Bachelors Degree, Project Manager, Agile, Vendor Management Experience Interperson Start date: 11/9/2026 End Date : 09/30/2027 Submission deadline: 10/16/2026 10:00:00 AM Client Info: EPMO Note: *- Interview Process: 1st round interviews will be virtual, but 2nd round interviews may take place in-person. Candidates MUST be available for an in-person interview. *- Hybrid: Resource will be working a hybrid schedule. NO REMOTE ONLY OPTION. Will need to be onsite from day 1, two days a week. *- Local candidates ONLY. Candidates must me located within 90 miles of Lansing, MI at time of submission. Description: This position provides oversight, leadership, accountability, and project management functions for large strategic and complex projects supporting Department of Information, Technology, and Budget (DTMB-MB) with high visibility at the Agency Executive level. These projects typically have a large diverse set of stakeholders, utilize vendor participation, require coordination of multiple stakeholders, complex schedules, and significant integration with other systems. Advanced experience managing complex projects, a significant degree of creativity and latitude is required. Works under limited supervision with considerable latitude for the use of initiative and independent judgment. - Minimum of six years of professional experience as a project manager for IT software or infrastructure projects involving 50 or more team members. - Advanced experience managing Agile projects - Advanced experience managing scope, schedule, and project budget - Advanced experience with vendor management - Experience writing or participating in development of Statement of Work (SOW), Request for Proposal (RFP) or contracts - Strong leadership, communication, and interpersonal skills - Possession of a PMP Certification is highly desired",
