    "description": "Engineer: OLAP, API, ETL Process, JSON XML Advanced ESB JavaScript 1.2 Gro Start date :9/28/2026 End Date: 02/21/2027 Submission deadline : 10/6/2026 Client Info : NCDHHS-NCFAST Note: *Hybrid *Either Webcam Interview or In Person Description: The NC Department of Health and Human Services seeks a highly technical resources to serve as a Data Integration, API and ETL developer for creating real-time, on-demand, batch and scheduled data interfaces and processing between systems and applications, both internal and external. This Integration/Interface engineer position must be very well organized and able to manage multiple business, technical, and validation efforts. The candidate must have experience in solutioning from both a technical and functional perspective and must be able to understand and help clarify client requirements, design, and build the solution leveraging multiple resources/teams utilizing Salesforce and other platforms. The engineer must participate in exploring business needs, architectural analysis, development, testing, production support, and system maintenance. Duties include requirements gathering, designing, and implementing solutions, and supporting go-live and post-implementation. The Integration/Interface engineer position has responsibility for providing hands-on development, design, implementation, and support of business solutions based on MuleSoft technology. Must have experience in MuleSoft architecture principles, system integration, technical sizing, high availability aspects, and integration best practices. In addition to MuleSoft experience (a must have skill), preference would be for candidates with experience in designing and developing integration solutions using IIB/ACE or Boomi.",
