    "description": "Manager: Data Governance, Data Management, State Government Experience., Project Management Experience Start date :10/19/2026 End Date :06/30/2027 Submission deadline :10/05/2026 Client Info :TN F&A STS Note: * Position Location: Hybrid * Candidate Must Be Local Description: The Enterprise Data Governance Consultant will support the State of Tennessee Center for Enterprise Data & Analytics (CEDA) in expanding enterprise data governance services, AI data preparations, training, communications, stakeholder engagement, and agency implementation support. This contractor position will work under the direction of the Enterprise Data Governance Manager helping agencies and departments establish, mature, and sustain data governance programs. The role supports Tennessees enterprise approach to managing data as a strategic asset, improving trusted data use, reducing risk, enabling secure data sharing, and increasing efficiency through standardization. The States Enterprise Data Governance Program is built around a coordinated Framework, Guidebook, and Playbook that define the “why,” “what,” and “how” of statewide data governance implementation. This position is intended for a consultant with strong public-sector facilitation, AI governance, change management, training, communications, and data governance implementation skills. The consultant will help translate governance concepts into practical agency actions, including data strategy development, governance meeting facilitation, stakeholder engagement, maturity assessments, implementation planning, training delivery, and program communications. Primary Responsibilities: AI Governance, Privacy, Risk, and Compliance Support The contractor will help agencies incorporate responsible AI, privacy, security, and compliance considerations into data governance practices. Responsibilities include: Support agency awareness of AI governance concepts, including ethical, transparent, explainable, accountable, and human-reviewed use of data and AI-enabled systems. Help document AI-related data use cases, data sources, stewardship responsibilities, risk considerations, and governance checkpoints. Coordinate with appropriate privacy, security, legal, records, and compliance stakeholders when governance activities involve sensitive, confidential, regulated, or high-risk data. Facilitate agency exploitation of AI technologies to establish practitioners to automate and/or streamline data governance practices and artifacts. Reinforce requirements for data classification, access management, data minimization, authorized use, retention, and secure data sharing. Support documentation of data-related risks, issues, policy exceptions, remediation actions, and audit evidence. Promote appropriate safeguards for protected or regulated data, including HIPAA, FERPA, CJIS, IRS Pub. 1075, PCI, FTI, PII, and other applicable standards when relevant to agency operations. Data Governance Strategy and Agency Engagement The contractor will help agencies align data governance activities to business value, mission priorities, compliance needs, and statewide data strategy. Responsibilities include: Support agency data governance planning, including charters, roadmaps, operating models, stakeholder maps, and implementation plans. Assist agencies in defining data governance scope, ownership, roles, responsibilities, decision rights, and engagement processes. Help identify agency value-based business needs, data pain points, data quality risks, and opportunities for improved data sharing and reuse. Support agency maturity assessments and develop practical work plans to close governance gaps. Translate technical data governance concepts into plain-language guidance suitable for executives, business program staff, data stewa",
