    "description": "Tester: Software Quality Assurance, Jira, KOFAX, Case Management Start date: 10/19/2026 End Date : 01/31/2027 Submission deadline: 10/02/2026 Client Info: GDOL Note: * Work Arrangement: Onsite * Agency Interview Type: Either Web Cam or In Person Description: Key Responsibilities * Test Case Authoring: Design, write, and maintain comprehensive, clear, and reusable test cases, scenarios, and test plans based on business requirements, system specifications, and integration flows. * Interface & Integration Testing: Author detailed test cases covering end-to-end interface testing, API integrations, data exchanges, and communication channels between system components. * Kofax Testing: Design specialized test scenarios for Kofax capture, transformation, and document processing solutions, ensuring seamless data extraction, validation, and workflow routing. * Requirements Analysis: Collaborate closely with product managers, developers, and stakeholders to understand feature requirements and identify edge cases early in the development lifecycle. * Test Management: Organize, structure, and maintain all testing documentation and traceability matrices using XRAY and Jira. * Minimal Execution: Perform exploratory or targeted validation only when strictly necessary, focusing the vast majority of your effort on robust test strategy and documentation. * Required Skills & Qualifications Experience: 4 to 6 years of software quality assurance experience in an Agile environment. Technical Stack Knowledge: Solid understanding of testing web applications built on Angular (front end) and Java (backend/micro services architectures). Specialized Testing Expertise: Demonstrated experience in designing test cases for Interface Testing (APIs, web services, system-to-system integrations). Hands-on test design experience with Kofax capture and document automation solutions. Tool Expertise: Extensive experience with Jira for tracking and requirement alignment. Proficiency in XRAY for test case management, execution mapping, and requirements traceability. Technical Acumen: Ability to review technical specifications, API payloads, and component interactions to craft precise, high-value test cases. Communication: Exceptional written and verbal communication skills to articulate complex test scenarios clearly to developers and stakeholders.",
