    "description": "Manager: Program Management, IT Modernization, Reengineering Experience, Mapping Strong Facilitation Skills Commu Start date: 10/12/2026 End Date: 10/11/2027 Submission deadline: 10/02/2026 Client Info: SCC Note: *Deadline to submit: Friday, Oct 2 by 4 pm est ONSITE REQ: Minimum 3 days onsite but can vary which days depending on meeting schedules. Parking is NOT provided for contractors. Note: Active PMP cert is REQUIRED! CSM and SAFe are most desired addl certs with the others (CSPO, PSPO, SAFe POPM, CSM, Lean Six Sigma, ITIL Foundation, or other Agile/product credentials) nice to have. Pls upload under the reference tab Work Arrangement: Hybrid Agency Interview Type: Web Cam Interview Only Description: The SCC is looking for a PM to manage the transition to a new Banking partner for all its divisions and functions that either collect revenue, perform or support deposit duties and/or other monies processing in any capacity for the SCC (7 divisions). This will require managing the overall deliverables and resources from all stakeholders, which include the selected Banking partner resources, the SCC representatives from each Revenue collecting division (6), OCC (Office of Commission Comptroller) and ETS (Enterprise Technology Services). As new technology and services will be deployed a key component will be to ensure a complete set of requirements are documented up front for each division. In addition, this role will need to facilitate and support the divisions to identify changes in current processes needed to streamline activities and take full advantage of the new technology available from the selected Banking partner.",
