    "description": "Consultant: Project ,Management Experience, IT Project Experience, Project Management, PowerBI Dash Boarding Start date :11/2/2026 End Date :12 Months from projected start date Submission deadline :10/2/2026 5:00:00 PM Client Info : DPH Note: *Interview Process: 2 Rounds of Virtual Interviews *Possibility for Extension: Yes *Work Location: Hybrid. Onsite expectations depend upon project needs and can be expected to range between once per month and once per quarter with little notice. *Candidate location: Candidate must be a CURRENT SC resident. No relocation allowed. Description: At the SC Department of Public Health (SC DPH), we are committed to helping people live healthier lives in thriving communities. With a workforce of over 3,000 professionals across 70 locations statewide, our agency is powered by a diverse team of experts who are passionate about making a meaningful impact. Why is this position open (new role, increased workload, new dept, resignation, promotion)? The role provides oversight and coordination of agency-wide initiatives, ensuring effective resource management, project governance, and successful project delivery. Continued support in this capacity is essential to maintain operational continuity, advancing strategic initiatives, and ensuring the successful execution of the agencys project portfolio. Scope of the project: This position supports the agencys project management and governance functions, including implementation of the new Project Management System, portfolio oversight, dashboard reporting, user training, and stakeholder support. As the PWA is decommissioned, the role will provide expertise in system implementation, project visibility, organizational change management, and leadership of strategic projects aligned with the South Carolina Department of Public Health. Daily Duties / Responsibilities: Responsibilities include supporting large-scale technology and business projects, maintaining project management standards and best practices, facilitating stakeholder engagement, and enhancing project management maturity across the organization. Work Mode (Hybrid, Onsite, Remote): Hybrid, onsite presence is based on project needs and can be anticipated to be between once per month and once per quarter.",
