    "description": "Tech Lead: SHARE POINT, Microsoft 365, SharePoint Framework, Implementing SharePoint Solutions Workfl Start date: 11/03/2026 End Date : 12 Months from projected start date Submission deadline: 10/1/2026 5:00:00 PM Client Info: SCDMV Note: *On Site *Experienced Non-manager. *Interview Process: 1 Virtual followed by 1 Onsite Interview *Possibility for Extension: No - this is for a project that has an anticipated timeline of 12 months *Work Location: Fully Onsite. No flexibility for hybrid or remote. *Candidate location: Candidate must be a CURRENT resident of SC, NC, or GA and willing to relocate to SC at their own expense. Description: Please ensure you attach the SC Cover Sheet (attached), a valid Right to Represent, and the candidates resume with full legal first name, and last name. Posting attachments should be named as Attachment Name, Posting ID, Last Name, First Name. Ex: Resume_1234_Last_First, RTR_1234_Last_First, Coversheet_1234_Last_First Withdrawn candidates will not be permitted to be replaced. If you would like to use a sub vendor, only 1 level deep, please submit the Sub Vendor usage form. Fingerprinting must take place in South Carolina at least five (5) business days prior to the start date Scope Of The Project The purpose of this engagement is to obtain a qualified SharePoint Online Administrator to plan, design, administer, modernize, and optimize SCDMVs SharePoint Online sites, flows, and configuration. The SharePoint Online Administrator will merge SharePoint Online technical capabilities with SCDMV business goals and objectives to produce a platform for the agency to further its mission of delivering exceptional customer service and promoting effective and efficient business processes, professional employees, innovative technology, and strategic partnerships. Daily Duties: The SharePoint Online Administrator will report to the Server Team Manager within the Server Team. The SharePoint Online Administrator will work with Server Team members, Business Unit Directors, Managers, and their staff. The SharePoint Online Administrator will provide both front-end support to all end users and collaborate with business units to enhance functionality, governance, user experience, advanced permissions, and operational efficiency. This includes designing and developing intranet solutions, including custom layouts, workflows, and automation. Strong UI/UX design skills and the ability to create user-friendly, accessible interfaces are needed. This role delivers modern, scalable solutions using SharePoint Online and Microsoft 365 tools, collaborating with cross-functional teams to automate business processes, ensure secure and accessible systems, and enhance the SCDMV SharePoint Online tenant as new features become available and other features are deprecated. Ultimately, the contractor will become a champion of the capabilities of SharePoint Online, advance SCDMVs understanding of what can be achieved by utilizing SharePoint Online and increase functionality and usage. Responsibilities: • Design, administer, and maintain the functionality of sites, subsites, and links. • Use best practices within Entra ID architecture to design, administer, and manage security groups, advanced settings, and permissions in SharePoint Online, including site permissions for streamlining owner, member, and visitor roles. • Perform site and content permission audits as defined by the agency. • Work with site owners to increase the functionality of departmental SharePoint Online sites and subsites. • Manage site layout structure, content, workflows, and automation. • Provide SharePoint Online support to end users. • Provide functionality training to the training department and end users. • Review and monitor usage reports. • Clean up sites and remove unused sites. • Create and maintain detailed documentation of SharePoint Online services and setti",
