    "description": "Developer: Excel, Python, Data Manipulation, Data Analysis Start date: 10/05/2026 End Date : 12/31/2026 Submission deadline: 09/28/2026 Client Info: CT DPH Note: *Hybrid *Candidate Must Be Local *Occasionally, work may be performed onsite at 410 Capitol Avenue, Hartford; otherwise, the work will be remote (as determined by the Point of Contact). *All work shall occur between the hours of 8:00 am and 5:00 pm on official workdays in the State of Connecticut or as otherwise approved by the Point of Contact. Description: The Connecticut Department of Public Health (CT-DPH) aims to predict, prevent, detect, and respond to public health threats faster and more efficiently than ever before. Under this initiative, CT-DPH is committed to achieving this vision by developing and deploying approaches that move the public health community from siloed and brittle public health data systems to connected, resilient, adaptable, and sustainable response-ready systems capable of meeting today and tomorrows health challenges. (Data Modernization Initiative (DMI) Program Overview Various sections and programs currently track and manage critical information through disparate Excel files and Word documents. This manual, unstructured approach creates compliance risks, missed deadlines, and limited data visibility. Transitioning from a paper-based workflow to an automated Microsoft Power BI ecosystem through a Data Submissions and CGMS Portal has been a comprehensive, modernized, and successful strategy. The core program goals focus on eliminating manual data entry, enforcing data governance, and providing stakeholders with real-time decision-support capabilities and data analytics. Workstream Overview – (CGMS) Contracts, Grants, Management System The (CGMS) Contracting process manages the full lifecycle of contract development and execution, progressing through the following key stages. The current environment combines manual and system-assisted processes that support the full lifecycle of grants, contracting, financial reporting, and payment/refund activities. The process begins with the Contractor Information Intake process and moves through the below steps/phases, ending with the routing, approval, and execution phase. · Contractor Information Intake: Program initiates the process by providing contractor details and required supporting documentation. · Electronic Department Agreement Request (EDAR) Checklist Preparation: Program compiles and validates all required documentation, approvals, and data elements necessary for contract routing. · Electronic Department Agreement Request (EDAR) Submission: The formal contract request is submitted through the EDAR system, including fiscal data, contract type, and supporting materials for CMS review. · Legal Review & Contract Language: Contract language is reviewed and revised collaboratively by Legal, Program, and CMS. · Contract Development & Initiation: CMS prepares the appropriate contract template and ensures readiness for execution. · Routing, Approval & Execution: The Contract Specialist manages approvals, signatures, and final contract execution and distribution. About the Role: We are seeking (1) skilled Power BI Analyst. The Power BI Analyst will work with the Information Technology (IT) development team, in collaboration with Business Analysts, Quality Assurance Testers, Trainers, and the Production Support Information Technology team. The Power BI Analyst will design, build, and manage data models, interactive dashboards, and reports in Power BI to turn raw data into clear business insights and analyses that support leadership in evaluating key performance metrics, modeling behaviors, and data. Core Responsibilities: Data Preparation: Clean, transform, and shape raw datasets using Power Query and SQL. Data Modeling: Build stable",
