    "description": "===============================================================\n📌 POSITION & CLIENT OVERVIEW\n===============================================================\n• Position Title: Enterprise Architect (165118)\n• Client / Agency: State Client\n• Work Arrangement: Hybrid\n• Interview Type: Webcam / In-Person\n• Target Start Date: 10/05/2026\n• Target End Date: 1 Years from projected start date\n• Submission Deadline: 9/4/2026 4:00:00 PM\n\n===============================================================\n🎯 PROJECT SUMMARY & OBJECTIVE\n===============================================================\nThe Data Governance Operations Support role will provide tactical coordination and operational support to ensure DG pilots, intake processes, standards rollouts and DG related project work more efficiently across business, IT, and program stakeholders. This role will also work with North Dakota Information Technology (NDIT) to ensure alignment with statewide data governance efforts, policies, standards, etc.\n\n===============================================================\n📋 KEY ROLES & RESPONSIBILITIES\n===============================================================\n• For your bid to be complete you must include the following:\no A valid Right to Represent (See vendor information page for RTR requirements)\no Your candidates resume with full legal first name and last name.\no North Dakota Candidate Cover sheet (attached)\n\nYears of Experience: We are looking for a resource with senior-level experience, given the need to support governance operations, intake and prioritization, and the repeatable processes\n5+ years in program coordination or governance operations, data management, business operations or related enterprise support\nExperience working across IT and business stakeholders\nStrong documentation and process management skills\n\nResponsibilities:\n• Coordinate pilot implementation across programs\n• Support governance intake workflows and follow-up actions\n• Track checklist compliance, onboarding progress and standards adoption.\n• Support modernization projects with embedded Data Governance guidance\n• Maintain documentation, reporting, meeting notes, and action items tracking.\n• Coordinate with data stewards, business teams, IT and project stakeholders.\n• 5-10 years experience with program coordination, governance operations, data management, or business operations.\n• Strong documentation, tracking, and follow-up skills.\n• Ability to coordinate across business and IT stakeholders.\n• Ability to communicate effectively with technical and non-technical audiences.\n• Experience with Health and Human Services, public sector, or large enterprise environments.\n• Experience supporting modernization, reporting, data governance, or standards related initiatives.\n• Education: Bachelors degree in related field such as computer science.\n• One of the following certifications is highly desired: CDMP, PMP, or equivalent data governance/project management certification.\n• Once they have provided results, MSP Delivery Specialist will indicate status on the Onboarding Checklist.\n\n===============================================================\n🛠️ REQUIRED TECHNICAL PROFICIENCIES\n===============================================================\n• Program Coordinator\n• Governance\n• Data Management\n• SQL Analyst Data Quality Analyst\n\n===============================================================\n🌟 PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS & DOMAIN SKILLS\n===============================================================\n• Preferred skills that stand out on resume\n• Familiarity with dashboards, data inventories, business glossaries, metadata, data quality tracking, SQL or data queries.\n• Preferred certifications include:\nDAMA Certified Data Management Professional (CDMP)\nDCAM Certification\nPMP or CAPM\n\nSecurity Comments: State of North Dakota conducts fingerprinting and all on boarding compliance.",
    "rawDescription": "Architect: Program Coordinator, Governance, Data Management, SQL Analyst Data Quality Analyst\n\nStart date :10/05/2026\nEnd Date :1 Years from projected start date\n\nSubmission deadline: 9/4/2026 4:00:00 PM\n\nClient Info: ITS\n\nNote:\n*Position place: Hybrid preferred\n*Remote may be considered.\n*State of North Dakota conducts fingerprinting and all on boarding compliance.\n\nDescription:\nThe Data Governance Operations Support role will provide tactical coordination and operational support to ensure DG pilots, intake processes, standards rollouts and DG related project work more efficiently across business, IT, and program stakeholders. This role will also work with North Dakota Information Technology (NDIT) to ensure alignment with statewide data governance efforts, policies, standards, etc.\n\nFor your bid to be complete you must include the following:\no A valid Right to Represent (See vendor information page for RTR requirements)\no Your candidates resume with full legal first name and last name.\no North Dakota Candidate Cover sheet (attached)\n\nYears of Experience: We are looking for a resource with senior-level experience, given the need to support governance operations, intake and prioritization, and the repeatable processes\n5+ years in program coordination or governance operations, data management, business operations or related enterprise support\nExperience working across IT and business stakeholders\nStrong documentation and process management skills\n\nResponsibilities:\n• Coordinate pilot implementation across programs\n• Support governance intake workflows and follow-up actions\n• Track checklist compliance, onboarding progress and standards adoption.\n• Support modernization projects with embedded Data Governance guidance\n• Maintain documentation, reporting, meeting notes, and action items tracking.\n• Coordinate with data stewards, business teams, IT and project stakeholders.\n\nRequired Skills:\n• 5-10 years experience with program coordination, governance operations, data management, or business operations.\n• Strong documentation, tracking, and follow-up skills.\n• Ability to coordinate across business and IT stakeholders.\n• Ability to communicate effectively with technical and non-technical audiences.\n\nPreferred skills that stand out on resume\n• Experience with Health and Human Services, public sector, or large enterprise environments.\n• Experience supporting modernization, reporting, data governance, or standards related initiatives.\n• Familiarity with dashboards, data inventories, business glossaries, metadata, data quality tracking, SQL or data queries.\n\nEducation: Bachelors degree in related field such as computer science.\nOne of the following certifications is highly desired: CDMP, PMP, or equivalent data governance/project management certification.\nPreferred certifications include:\nDAMA Certified Data Management Professional (CDMP)\nDCAM Certification\nPMP or CAPM\n\nSecurity Comments: State of North Dakota conducts fingerprinting and all on boarding compliance. Once they have provided results, MSP Delivery Specialist will indicate status on the Onboarding Checklist.",
