    "description": "===============================================================\n📌 POSITION & CLIENT OVERVIEW\n===============================================================\n• Position Title: Enterprise Project Manager - Advanced (13421)\n• Client / Agency: ADMIN\n• Work Arrangement: Onsite\n• Interview Type: Process: 1 round, Virtual/Online\n• Target Start Date: 9/28/2026\n• Target End Date: 12 Months from projected start date\n• Submission Deadline: 09/08 at 5:00 PM EST.\n\n===============================================================\n🎯 PROJECT SUMMARY & OBJECTIVE\n===============================================================\nProject Overview\n\n\n\nClient requires professional services to support the successful delivery of strategic and tactical IT initiatives. The Contractor will provide a Project Manager with strong business analysis capabilities to lead and support complex, multi-stakeholder technology projects from initiation through closure.\n\n===============================================================\n📋 KEY ROLES & RESPONSIBILITIES\n===============================================================\n• The role will ensure clear requirements, well-defined scope, effective communication, and disciplined project execution.\n• Scope of the project:\n\n\n\nThe primary objectives of this engagement are:\n• Deliver project outcomes on time, within scope, and within budget.\n• Provide expert-level project management to guide planning, scheduling, execution, risk mitigation, and reporting.\n• Provide business analysis expertise to define and document requirements, assess impacts, and ensure solutions meet business needs.\n• Improve project transparency through accurate documentation, dashboards, and communication to leadership and stakeholders.\n• The Contractor will report to the Director of Admin IT or designated project executive.\n• Regular updates will be required through established reporting mechanisms and recurring meetings.\n• Daily Duties / Responsibilities:\n\n\n\nProject Management Responsibilities\n• Lead end-to-end project delivery, including scope, schedule, budget, risk, quality, communication, and resource coordination\n• Develop and maintain project plans, RAID logs, communication plans, status reports, and executive updates\n• Manage cross-functional teams including internal IT, vendors, SMEs, and agency partners.\n• Facilitate work sessions to validate scope, requirements, and deliverables; maintain alignment with sponsors and stakeholders\n• Identify risks and issues; recommend and implement mitigation strategies\n• Support procurement processes as needed (RFPs, SOWs, vendor oversight) consistent with state and Admin procurement standard\n• Ensure compliance with agency policies, security requirements, records management standards, and project governance frameworks\n\n\n\nBusiness Analysis Responsibilities:\n• Lead structured requirements elicitation including interviews, workshops, journey mapping, process modeling, and data analysis\n• Document clear, testable requirements: business, functional, nonfunctional, user stories, and acceptance criteria.\n• Define current-state and future-state processes, workflows, and data flows; quantify KPIs and business value.\n• Translate requirements into solution designs in collaboration with architecture, security, data, and infrastructure teams.\n• Evaluate build-vs-buy options and support creation of diagrams, models, and integration patterns when required.\n• Change Management & Adoption\n• Develop change management and communication plans.\n• Coordinate UAT, cutover activities, readiness planning, and post-launch support.\n• Support adoption using metrics, user feedback, and continuous improvement loops\n\nDocumentation Deliverables\n\nDeliverables may include but are not limited to:\n• Project Charter\n• Requirements Documents / User Stories\n• Process Diagrams\n\n===============================================================\n🛠️ REQUIRED TECHNICAL PROFICIENCIES\n===============================================================\n• Core Technical Proficiency in required functional & technical domain\n• Experience with system architecture, workflow design, and access controls\n• Strong problem-solving, documentation, and stakeholder collaboration capabilities",
