    "description": "===============================================================\n📌 POSITION & CLIENT OVERVIEW\n===============================================================\n• Position Title: NC DHHS AWS Senior Developer (808496)\n• Client / Agency: NCDHHS-PMO\n• Work Arrangement: Hybrid\n• Interview Type: or In Person\n• Target Start Date: 09/08/2026\n• Target End Date: 09/07/2027\n• Submission Deadline: 09/09/2026\n\n===============================================================\n🎯 PROJECT SUMMARY & OBJECTIVE\n===============================================================\nExperience in modernizing legacy applications, which should include refactoring/migrating in-house legacy applications to the cloud environment. Experience in customizing AWS ETL logic using Python code.\n\n===============================================================\n📋 KEY ROLES & RESPONSIBILITIES\n===============================================================\n• DHHS-ITD is looking to hire a senior AWS developer with 10-15 years of software development experience.\n• This role involves close collaboration with the data modernization teams at ITD and DPH to design, implement, and manage AWS solutions.\n• Skill Sets and experience includes:\n\n\n\nExtensive experience in developing/ building AWS Data Lake formation, contributing extensively to design, development and writing code.\n• Knowledgeable and experience in security and data governance covering areas such as fine-grained permissions, managing user and service permissions, data encryption, auditing, and compliance.\n• Experience in software development with hands-on skills in Python scripting, and any prior experience in Object oriented languages is a plus.\n• Experience working with any transactional or RDMS databases\n\nExperience with DevOps, DevSecOps, Iac, automation, building CI/CD pipelines, monitoring, and logging.\n• Knowledge / experience using any ETL tools, experience with data analytics using PowerBI or AWS QuickSight etc. is plus.\n• Job responsibilities include (but not limited to):\n• Collaborating with stakeholders to gather requirements and propose effective modernization strategies\n• Providing technical guidance and troubleshooting support throughout project delivery\n• Acting as a trusted advisor to the technical team on industry trends and emerging technologies\n• Develop, test, debug and deliver within timeline using best tools and best practices available.\n• Ability to identify, analyze, and resolve technical issues and challenges.\n• Designing and implementing complex, scalable, and secure AWS solutions tailored to customer needs\n• Identifies architectural risks and plans to mitigate risks\n• Ensures adherence to standards and best practices\n• Influences and communicates effectively with non-technical audiences including senior ITD and business stakeholders.\n\n===============================================================\n🛠️ REQUIRED TECHNICAL PROFICIENCIES\n===============================================================\n• Proficient in utilizing AWS services and related components towards building enterprise level Data Lakes.\n• Must have experience in Data Ingestion & Storage, Data Processing & Transformation and working with AWS Machine Language using appropriate AWS services.\n• Must have experience/familiar with Agile/Scrum Framework environments.",
    "rawDescription": "Developer: VPC, ECS, EKS, WAF, Peering, API Gateway, Data Ingestion, Java J2EE\n\nStart Date: 09/08/2026\n\nEnd Date:   09/07/2027\n\n\n\nSubmission Deadline: 09/09/2026\n\n\n\nClient info: NCDHHS-PMO\n\n\n\nNote:\n\n*Hybrid\n\n*Either Webcam Interview or In Person\n\n\t\n\nDescription:\n\n\n\nDHHS-ITD is looking to hire a senior AWS developer with 10-15 years of software development experience. This role involves close collaboration with the data modernization teams at ITD and DPH to design, implement, and manage AWS solutions.\n\n\n\nSkill Sets and experience includes:\n\n\n\nExtensive experience in developing/ building AWS Data Lake formation, contributing extensively to design, development and writing code.\n\nExperience in modernizing legacy applications, which should include refactoring/migrating in-house legacy applications to the cloud environment.\n\nProficient in utilizing AWS services and related components towards building enterprise level Data Lakes.\n\nMust have experience in Data Ingestion & Storage, Data Processing & Transformation and working with AWS Machine Language using appropriate AWS services.\n\nExperience in customizing AWS ETL logic using Python code.\n\nKnowledgeable and experience in security and data governance covering areas such as fine-grained permissions, managing user and service permissions, data encryption, auditing, and compliance.\n\nExperience in software development with hands-on skills in Python scripting, and any prior experience in Object oriented languages is a plus.\n\nExperience working with any transactional or RDMS databases\n\nExperience with DevOps, DevSecOps, Iac, automation, building CI/CD pipelines, monitoring, and logging.\n\nKnowledge / experience using any ETL tools, experience with data analytics using PowerBI or AWS QuickSight etc. is plus.\n\nMust have experience/familiar with Agile/Scrum Framework environments.\n\n\n\n Job responsibilities include (but not limited to):\n\n\n\n• Collaborating with stakeholders to gather requirements and propose effective modernization strategies\n\n\n\n• Providing technical guidance and troubleshooting support throughout project delivery\n\n\n\n• Acting as a trusted advisor to the technical team on industry trends and emerging technologies\n\n\n\n• Develop, test, debug and deliver within timeline using best tools and best practices available.\n\n\n\n• Ability to identify, analyze, and resolve technical issues and challenges.\n\n\n\n• Designing and implementing complex, scalable, and secure AWS solutions tailored to customer needs\n\n\n\n• Identifies architectural risks and plans to mitigate risks\n\n\n\n• Ensures adherence to standards and best practices\n\n\n\n• Influences and communicates effectively with non-technical audiences including senior ITD and business stakeholders.",
