    "status": "Closed",
    "description": "===============================================================\n📌 POSITION & CLIENT OVERVIEW\n===============================================================\n• Position Title: DHHS MS Power Platform Developer Architect (805119)\n• Client / Agency: NCDHHS-PH\n• Work Arrangement: Hybrid\n• Interview Type: Either Webcam Interview or In Person\n• Target Start Date: 07/13/2026\n• Target End Date: 07/12/2027\n• Submission Deadline: 09/03/2026\n\n===============================================================\n🎯 PROJECT SUMMARY & OBJECTIVE\n===============================================================\nThis position is needed to create a system to be used for statewide billing for establishments holding food, lodging, pool and tattoo permits. An existing software is end of life and due to be deprecated.\n\n===============================================================\n📋 KEY ROLES & RESPONSIBILITIES\n===============================================================\n• The resource will be tasked with recreating the functionality of that system in Power Platform.\n• Responsibilities\n\n\n\nElements of the system will include: a pipeline to mirror SQL data held in an AWS hosted cloud DB down to Dataverse, where the lists of active facilities can be extracted to serve as the census for establishments to be billed.\n• Automations linked to Dynamics records will create invoices, send them to email addresses on file, and track payments received or outstanding.\n• To facilitate the online payments, PayIt will beleveraged.\n• We can direct payees to PayIt via their invoice emails, and PayItwill provide a report back to Dynamics to be consumed and converted into Payments records, corresponding to open Invoices which can then be marked closed.\n• Some payments will be received by check, in which case the Dynamics system will need to be capable of logging checks received, submitted to the controller, and reconciled in order to square our records to NCFS.\n• All communication around invoicing is to take place through the case management system, logging calls and emails with relationships defined to associated records (Contact, Case, Invoice for example).\n• A reporting system will be needed to look at invoicing metrics and program performance.\n• An essential requirement will be the creation of a robust ALM system using 3environments (Development, UAT and PROD) where guids and other components are synchronized throughout to allow for seamless promotion of new functionality.\n• Qualifications:\n• Bachelors degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related field.\n• At least 3 years of experience in MS Power Platform development and implementation.\n• Proficiency in PowerApps, Power Virtual Agent, and Dataverse.\n• Knowledge of SQL database structure.\n• Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\n• Excellent verbal and written communication skills.\n• Ability to work independently and as part of a team.\n• Ability to prioritize tasks and manage time effectively.\n• If you have a passion for innovation and are driven to deliver exceptional results, we would love to hear from you.\n• This is a fantastic opportunity to be an active contributor to the development of public health infrastructure for the state of North Carolina\n\n===============================================================\n🛠️ REQUIRED TECHNICAL PROFICIENCIES\n===============================================================\n• Core Technical Proficiency in required functional & technical domain\n• Experience with system architecture, workflow design, and access controls\n• Strong problem-solving, documentation, and stakeholder collaboration capabilities\n\n===============================================================\n🌟 PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS & DOMAIN SKILLS\n===============================================================\n• Preferred: Microsoft Certification-Power Platform Developer Associate (PL-400) or higher",
    "rawDescription": "Architect: Computer Science, Information System, POWER VIRTUAL AGENT, Dataverse SQL Database\n\nStart date :07/13/2026\n\nEnd Date   :07/12/2027\n\n\n\nSubmission deadline :09/03/2026\n\n\n\nClient Info : NCDHHS-PH\n\n\n\n\n\nNote:\n\n* Work Arrangement: Hybrid\n\n\n\n* Agency Interview Type: Either Webcam Interview or In Person\n\n\n\n* We are seeking a highly skilled and motivated MS Power Platform Developer/Architect to join our team.\n\n\n\n\n\nDescription:\n\n\n\nThis position is needed to create a system to be used for statewide billing for establishments holding food, lodging, pool and tattoo permits. An existing software is end of life and due to be deprecated. The resource will be tasked with recreating the functionality of that system in Power Platform.\n\n\n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n\nElements of the system will include: a pipeline to mirror SQL data held in an AWS hosted cloud DB down to Dataverse, where the lists of active facilities can be extracted to serve as the census for establishments to be billed. Automations linked to Dynamics records will create invoices, send them to email addresses on file, and track payments received or outstanding.\n\n\n\nTo facilitate the online payments, PayIt will beleveraged. We can direct payees to PayIt via their invoice emails, and PayItwill provide a report back to Dynamics to be consumed and converted into Payments records, corresponding to open Invoices which can then be marked closed.\n\n\n\nSome payments will be received by check, in which case the Dynamics system will need to be capable of logging checks received, submitted to the controller, and reconciled in order to square our records to NCFS.\n\n\n\nAll communication around invoicing is to take place through the case management system, logging calls and emails with relationships defined to associated records (Contact, Case, Invoice for example).\n\n\n\nA reporting system will be needed to look at invoicing metrics and program performance.\n\nAn essential requirement will be the creation of a robust ALM system using 3environments (Development, UAT and PROD) where guids and other components are synchronized throughout to allow for seamless promotion of new functionality.\n\n\n\n* Qualifications:\n\n• Bachelors degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related field.\n\n• At least 3 years of experience in MS Power Platform development and implementation.\n\n• Proficiency in PowerApps, Power Virtual Agent, and Dataverse.\n\n• Knowledge of SQL database structure.\n\n• Preferred: Microsoft Certification-Power Platform Developer Associate (PL-400) or higher\n\n• Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\n\n• Excellent verbal and written communication skills.\n\n• Ability to work independently and as part of a team.\n\n• Ability to prioritize tasks and manage time effectively.\n\n\n\nIf you have a passion for innovation and are driven to deliver exceptional results, we would love to hear from you. This is a fantastic opportunity to be an active contributor to the development of public health infrastructure for the state of North Carolina",
