    "description": "===============================================================\n📌 POSITION & CLIENT OVERVIEW\n===============================================================\n• Position Title: Senior Salesforce Engineer (809821)\n• Client / Agency: NCDHHS-NCFAST\n• Work Arrangement: Hybrid\n• Interview Type: Either Webcam Interview or In Person\n• Target Start Date: 09/07/2026\n• Target End Date: 09/03/2027\n• Submission Deadline: 09/08/2026\n\n===============================================================\n🎯 PROJECT SUMMARY & OBJECTIVE\n===============================================================\nThe Department of Health and Human Services is seeking a contract Salesforce Solution Engineer to design and deliver end-to-end solutions on Salesforce Government Cloud for Child welfare program applications. This role supports mission-critical public-sector programs across case management, licensing, service operations, and related workflows.\n\n===============================================================\n📋 KEY ROLES & RESPONSIBILITIES\n===============================================================\n• The position ensures all solutions align with program objectives, technical standards, security requirements, and long-term platform strategy while leveraging both declarative and programmatic capabilities to build scalable, maintainable systems.\n• Key Responsibilities\n\n\n\nDiscovery and requirements: Lead technical discovery sessions with product owners and program stakeholders to define requirements, evaluate solution options, and recommend best-fit approaches.\n• Design and engineering: Lead integration designs, blueprinting and configuration strategies.\n• Development: Develop Apex, Lightning Web Components, Flows, and system integrations following established engineering practices and platform governance.\n• Release management readiness: Review Salesforce Spring, Summer, and Winter release notes to identify breaking changes, deprecations, new settings, and feature impacts.\n• Assessing platform updates affect existing systems and integrations.\n• AI-enablement: Apply AI-driven approaches to enhance Salesforce solutions, including identifying practical use cases, incorporating intelligent automation, and ensuring responsible and compliant use of emerging technologies.\n\n===============================================================\n🛠️ REQUIRED TECHNICAL PROFICIENCIES\n===============================================================\n• Core Technical Proficiency in required functional & technical domain\n• Experience with system architecture, workflow design, and access controls\n• Strong problem-solving, documentation, and stakeholder collaboration capabilities",
    "rawDescription": "Engineer: Customization, APEX, Design, \n\nStart date :09/07/2026\n\nEnd Date   :09/03/2027\n\n\n\nSubmission deadline :09/08/2026\n\n\n\nClient Info : NCDHHS-NCFAST\n\n\n\nNote:\n\n* Work Arrangement: Hybrid\n\n\n\n* Agency Interview Type: Either Webcam Interview or In Person\n\n\n\n\n\nDescription:\n\n\n\nThe Department of Health and Human Services is seeking a contract Salesforce Solution Engineer to design and deliver end-to-end solutions on Salesforce Government Cloud for Child welfare program applications. This role supports mission-critical public-sector programs across case management, licensing, service operations, and related workflows. The position ensures all solutions align with program objectives, technical standards, security requirements, and long-term platform strategy while leveraging both declarative and programmatic capabilities to build scalable, maintainable systems.\n\n\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n\n\nDiscovery and requirements: Lead technical discovery sessions with product owners and program stakeholders to define requirements, evaluate solution options, and recommend best-fit approaches.\n\n\n\nDesign and engineering: Lead integration designs, blueprinting and configuration strategies.\n\n\n\nDevelopment: Develop Apex, Lightning Web Components, Flows, and system integrations following established engineering practices and platform governance.\n\n\n\nRelease management readiness: Review Salesforce Spring, Summer, and Winter release notes to identify breaking changes, deprecations, new settings, and feature impacts. Assessing platform updates affect existing systems and integrations.\n\n\n\nAI-enablement: Apply AI-driven approaches to enhance Salesforce solutions, including identifying practical use cases, incorporating intelligent automation, and ensuring responsible and compliant use of emerging technologies.",
