    "description": "===============================================================\n📌 POSITION & CLIENT OVERVIEW\n===============================================================\n• Position Title: IT Data Analyst\n• Client / Agency: General Client\n• Work Arrangement: Remote\n• Interview Type: Webcam / In-Person\n\n===============================================================\n🎯 PROJECT SUMMARY & OBJECTIVE\n===============================================================\nAnalyst: Data Analyst, -, -, \n\nPlease find the project details below:\n\n\n\nProject Details:\n\n\n\nRole: Data Analyst / Business System Analyst\n\nLocation: Stamford, CT 06901 (Remote)\n\nDuration: 12 Months\n\nPosition Type: Contract\n\nJob Description\n\n\n\nRole: Data Analyst\n\n\n\nWe are seeking a highly experienced Data Analyst / Business System Analyst with over 3 years of experience in the Banking domain. The ideal candidate should have a strong background in both business and data analysis, along with hands-on experience in BFSI projects.\n\n===============================================================\n📋 KEY ROLES & RESPONSIBILITIES\n===============================================================\n• This role requires expertise in data analysis, data mapping, and close collaboration with development teams to ensure accurate implementation of business requirements.\n• Key Responsibilities:\n\n\n\nAnalyze source system data and map data attributes to target data models.\n• Develop comprehensive data mapping documents.\n• Define data transformation logic based on business requirements for source-to-target data mapping.\n• Collaborate with business users to gather, document, and define business requirements.\n• Prepare Functional Specification Documents (FSDs).\n• Work closely with development teams to ensure accurate implementation of business requirements.\n• Validate system implementations during System Integration Testing (SIT) and User Acceptance Testing (UAT) phases of the Software Development Lifecycle (SDLC).\n• Utilize AML monitoring tools such as Actimize, Oracle, SAS, etc., for effective monitoring and analysis.\n• Analyze transactional data, including Trades, Cash, Checks, ACH, Cards, Wires, Leases, and Loans.\n• Write SQL queries for data analysis, validation, and debugging.\n• Extensive knowledge and hands-on experience in Data Analysis.\n• Strong understanding of Data Management, including Data Quality and Exception Management.\n• Excellent SQL skills.\n• Knowledge of Python is an added advantage.\n• Experience working on large-scale projects and cross-functional teams.\n• Highly organized, proactive, responsive, and self-motivated with a positive attitude.\n• Work Environment:\n\n\n\nAbility to thrive in a fast-paced environment.\n• Quick learner with a self-starter mindset.\n\n===============================================================\n🛠️ REQUIRED TECHNICAL PROFICIENCIES\n===============================================================\n• Required Skills:\n\n\n\nBachelors degree with relevant 3 years experience in the Banking or Financial Services industry.",
    "rawDescription": "Analyst: Data Analyst, -, -, \n\nPlease find the project details below:\n\n\n\nProject Details:\n\n\n\nRole: Data Analyst / Business System Analyst\n\nLocation: Stamford, CT 06901 (Remote)\n\nDuration: 12 Months\n\nPosition Type: Contract\n\nJob Description\n\n\n\nRole: Data Analyst\n\n\n\nWe are seeking a highly experienced Data Analyst / Business System Analyst with over 3 years of experience in the Banking domain. The ideal candidate should have a strong background in both business and data analysis, along with hands-on experience in BFSI projects. This role requires expertise in data analysis, data mapping, and close collaboration with development teams to ensure accurate implementation of business requirements.\n\n\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n\n\nAnalyze source system data and map data attributes to target data models.\n\nDevelop comprehensive data mapping documents.\n\nDefine data transformation logic based on business requirements for source-to-target data mapping.\n\nCollaborate with business users to gather, document, and define business requirements.\n\nPrepare Functional Specification Documents (FSDs).\n\nWork closely with development teams to ensure accurate implementation of business requirements.\n\nValidate system implementations during System Integration Testing (SIT) and User Acceptance Testing (UAT) phases of the Software Development Lifecycle (SDLC).\n\nUtilize AML monitoring tools such as Actimize, Oracle, SAS, etc., for effective monitoring and analysis.\n\nAnalyze transactional data, including Trades, Cash, Checks, ACH, Cards, Wires, Leases, and Loans.\n\nWrite SQL queries for data analysis, validation, and debugging.\n\nRequired Skills:\n\n\n\nBachelors degree with relevant 3 years experience in the Banking or Financial Services industry.\n\nExtensive knowledge and hands-on experience in Data Analysis.\n\nStrong understanding of Data Management, including Data Quality and Exception Management.\n\nExcellent SQL skills.\n\nKnowledge of Python is an added advantage.\n\nExperience working on large-scale projects and cross-functional teams.\n\nHighly organized, proactive, responsive, and self-motivated with a positive attitude.\n\nWork Environment:\n\n\n\nAbility to thrive in a fast-paced environment.\n\nQuick learner with a self-starter mindset.",
