    "description": "===============================================================\n📌 POSITION & CLIENT OVERVIEW\n===============================================================\n• Position Title: NCDIT - Senior IT Project Manager (810423)\n• Client / Agency: State Client\n• Work Arrangement: Remote\n• Interview Type: Webcam Interview Only\n• Target Start Date: 09/01/2026\n• Target End Date: 06/30/2027\n• Submission Deadline: 08/31/2026\n\n===============================================================\n🎯 PROJECT SUMMARY & OBJECTIVE\n===============================================================\nThis 100% federally funded position is critical to the technical implementation of approximately 15 complex, high-impact projects underway, supporting three major Medicaid use cases. The projects are funded through an already approved Implementation Advance Planning Document (IAPD) with the federal Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) and NC Medicaid.\n\n===============================================================\n📋 KEY ROLES & RESPONSIBILITIES\n===============================================================\n• This Senior IT Project Manager position is critical in providing state oversight and coordination with vendor project managers.\n• The role also provides project management support for the HIEA team internally.\n• Without this critical, high-leverage role, there is a significant risk of poor project execution against the existing contracts, resulting in project delays and cost overruns, which ultimately support whole-person healthcare for Medicaid beneficiaries.\n\n===============================================================\n🛠️ REQUIRED TECHNICAL PROFICIENCIES\n===============================================================\n• UAT\n• Stakeholder Management\n• -",
