    "description": "===============================================================\n📌 POSITION & CLIENT OVERVIEW\n===============================================================\n• Position Title: ESL Teacher (66211)\n• Client / Agency: State Client\n• Work Arrangement: Hybrid\n• Interview Type: Webcam / In-Person\n• Target Start Date: 9/21/2026\n• Target End Date: 12/31/2026\n• Submission Deadline: 09/03/2026\n\n===============================================================\n🎯 PROJECT SUMMARY & OBJECTIVE\n===============================================================\nAn English as a Second Language (ESL) teacher for deaf and hard of hearing students specializes in creating learning environment tailored to the needs of students with a foundation in written or spoke language other than English who have hearing loss. This position currently serves two students for 1 hour a day 5 days a week.\n\n===============================================================\n📋 KEY ROLES & RESPONSIBILITIES\n===============================================================\n• The teacher develops individual learning plans (ILP), individualized lesson plans, adapts materials, and employs strategies to ensure that all students can participate fully in lessons and activities.\n• The number of students can change depending on enrollment.\n• The educator needs to have a background in American Sign Language usage and be able to sign.\n• Education:\n\nBachelors degree or higher\n\nValid Tennessee teaching license with an ESL endorsement\n\n===============================================================\n🛠️ REQUIRED TECHNICAL PROFICIENCIES\n===============================================================\n• Bachelors Degree\n• Teaching Skills\n• -",
