    "description": "Position Summary\n\n• The client is seeking an experienced Paralegal/Legal Secretary with 3-5 years of legal support experience to provide comprehensive litigation and administrative support to a team of 3-4 attorneys. The ideal candidate will have a strong understanding of the Florida court system, experience with court filings, case management, attorney calendar coordination, and litigation support functions.\n• This role requires a detail-oriented professional who can effectively manage multiple priorities, communicate with judicial assistants and court personnel, prepare legal documents, and support attorneys throughout the litigation process.\nKey Responsibilities\n\n• Provide legal secretarial and administrative support to assigned attorneys.\n• Format, proofread, finalize, type, and electronically file legal documents.\n• Prepare correspondence, pleadings, motions, notices, subpoenas, and other legal documents from drafts and templates.\n• File pleadings, motions, and other court documents with Florida Circuit Courts, DOAH, and other appropriate tribunals.\n• Maintain and organize attorney case files, both electronic and physical.\n• Manage attorney calendars, including scheduling hearings, depositions, mediations, trials, and client meetings.\n• Coordinate and communicate with Judicial Assistants regarding scheduling and court matters.\n• Assist attorneys with discovery requests, responses, and document production.\n• Prepare exhibits, hearing binders, and case-related documentation.\n• Arrange for service of process and maintain tracking of legal deadlines.\n• Retain and schedule court reporters and obtain hearing and deposition transcripts.\n• Monitor court dockets and case activities.\n• Perform general administrative duties, including answering phones, coordinating travel arrangements, and supporting office operations.\n• Assist with closing case files and records management activities.\nRequired Qualifications\n\n• 3-5 years of experience as a Paralegal, Legal Assistant, or Legal Secretary.\n• Experience supporting multiple attorneys simultaneously (3-4 attorneys preferred).\n• Knowledge of Florida court procedures, rules, and electronic filing systems.\n• Experience filing documents with Florida Circuit Courts.\n• Strong litigation support experience, including discovery, exhibits, and pleadings preparation.\n• Experience communicating with judges' offices and Judicial Assistants.\n• Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Outlook, Excel, PowerPoint).\n• Experience using Adobe Acrobat for document preparation and management.\n• Exceptional organizational, time management, and communication skills.\n• Ability to handle confidential information with professionalism and discretion.\n• Prior experience in a litigation practice environment.\n• Familiarity with court docketing systems and case management software.\n• Experience preparing trial exhibits and hearing materials.\n• Knowledge of e-filing requirements and court deadlines.\nSkills & Competencies\n\n• Litigation Support\n• Court Filings & E-Filing\n• Legal Document Preparation\n• Case Management\n• Calendar Management\n• Discovery Coordination\n• Pleadings & Motion Formatting\n• Court Scheduling\n• Records Management\n• Microsoft Office Suite\n• Adobe Acrobat\n• Written and Verbal Communication\n• Attention to Detail\n• Multitasking and Prioritization\nContract Position Requirements\n\n• The successful candidate will be responsible for supporting attorneys through all phases of litigation by managing court filings, maintaining case files, coordinating schedules, preparing legal documentation, and ensuring compliance with court deadlines and procedural requirements. This role demands strong organizational skills, accuracy, and the ability to thrive in a fast-paced legal environment.",
