    "description": "We are seeking an experienced Senior COBOL Developer to join our team in support of a large-scale, mission-critical core business system. This is a 12-month contract opportunity with a hybrid work schedule. The ideal candidate will have deep expertise in Visual/Micro Focus COBOL, strong Oracle SQL skills, and a proven track record of leading technical teams and delivering complex software solutions.\n\nWork Location & Schedule:\n\n• Hybrid position based in Blythewood, SC\n\n• Strong preference for fully onsite presence during the training period\n\n• After training, a schedule of up to two days remote per week may be discussed with the resource and hiring manager\n\n• Candidate MUST be a CURRENT SC, NC, or GA resident. May relocate at candidate's discretion to meet the hybrid work schedule prior to the start date at their own expense.\n\nInterview Process:\n\n• 2 rounds of virtual interviews\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n• Analyze the core business system and assigned tickets for development and/or system modification\n\n• Take the lead in analyzing and proposing solutions to assigned tickets and projects\n\n• Partner with business units to develop business specifications, translate them into technical specifications, and obtain business sign-off\n\n• Code, test, promote, and interact with impacted users to ensure solutions meet documented requirements\n\n• Provide production support for the core system\n\n• Deliver daily and weekly status updates to the development manager and business analysts\n\nRequired Skills & Experience:\n\n• 6+ years of experience with Visual and/or Micro Focus COBOL\n\n• Working knowledge of Visual COBOL V9\n\n• 10+ years of experience developing and maintaining complex, mission-critical applications in a Windows-based Client Server environment\n\n• 5+ years of experience leading a technical software development team in planning and deployment of software systems\n\n• 10+ years of experience coding and testing complex COBOL-based business systems in an Oracle SQL database and Windows-based client-server environment\n\n• 5+ years of experience providing Level 3 (L3) production support\n\n• 5+ years of experience functioning as the primary contact with business units to develop and review business and technical specifications and ensure delivery of specified functionality\n\n• 10+ years of experience with computer system analysis, design, coding, testing, debugging, and implementation techniques and practices for developing new systems or modifying existing systems\n\nPreferred Skills:\n\n• Oracle 19+ SQL\n\n• Familiarity with Microsoft Visual Studio .NET / C# development environment\n\n• Experience working in a governmental environment\n\n• Visual COBOL technical certifications\n\nAdditional Skills:\n\n• Experience mentoring and guiding less experienced technical colleagues\n\n• Proven proficiency communicating effectively with users, vendors, staff members, and management both orally and in writing\n\n• Ability to plan, define, lead, direct, instruct, and review project work and personnel\n\nEducation:\n\n• Bachelor's Degree in Computer Science or a closely related discipline preferred, with 10 years of experience\n\n• Experience in a government agency environment is extremely helpful",
