    "preferredSkills": [],
    "description": "Brief Description of Job Duties: \n\n• Coordinates and manages IT, administrative, program or operations related agency projects from initiation to completion, ensuring projects are delivered on time, within budget, and to the required standards to translate strategic goals into actionable plans.\n\nSpecified Duties: \n\nProject Approval and Prioritization \n\n•\tConsult with agency staff regarding the development of new projects.\n\n•\tSupport the agency’s Project Management Portfolio process through analysis, presentations, and reports for the agency’s leadership.\n\n•\tComplete the Planned Project Template for reportable projects.\n\nProject Planning\n\nDevelop or assist in the development of project plans (including schedules, Communication Plans, Quality Plans, Deliverable Definition Documents, etc.), budget requests, and management procedures.\n\n•\tInitiate project specific tools (such as MS Project and SharePoint) and practices within the State of Kansas guidelines which will be used to facilitate project tracking, reporting, and collaboration.\n\n•\tCoordinate and develop High Level and Detailed planning documents for reportable projects.\n\n•\tCoordinate and develop Federal Planning and Implementation Advanced Planning Documents (APD). \n\n•\tEvaluate project plans for compliance with architecture, standards, policies, and guidelines.\n\n•\tProvide IT project oversight to agency stakeholders and leadership for compliance with information technology planning guidelines, standards, policies and methodologies.\n\nProject Execution\n\n•\tManage IT project plans and coordinate the work of project members, internal and contracted, working on the project.\n\n•\tTrack project progress against established timeline, budget, and deliverable definitions.\n\n•\tMaintain project specific tools and practices to ensure effective project tracking, reporting, and collaboration.\n\n•\tIdentify, report, and facilitate the resolution of project deficiencies in the form of issues and risks.\n\n•\tConsult with agency stakeholders and leadership on progress of projects.\n\n•\tProvide project related presentations/briefings as required.\n\n•\tCoordinate and provide reporting on reportable projects\n\n•\tConduct lessons learned sessions and develop close out documentation.\n\nGeneral Duties\n\n•\tProvide support for the Project Management Office’s overall responsibilities, such as, agency project portfolio management, liaison and reporting requirements, and maintenance of agency project management tools.\n\n•\tAssist Project Analysts and other Project Managers as required. \n\n•\tOther duties as assigned.\n\nEducation Required: \n\n•\tHigh school diploma or GED\n\nPreferred Qualifications:\n\n•\tFour years of experience with IT-related project management\n\n•\tMust possess a certification or a traditional IT Project Management Methodology, such as the Project Management Professional (PMP) certification from the Project Management Institute (PMI)",
    "rawDescription": "<p><b>Brief Description of Job Duties:&nbsp;</b></p><p>• Coordinates and manages IT, administrative, program or operations related agency projects from initiation to completion, ensuring projects are delivered on time, within budget, and to the required standards to translate strategic goals into actionable plans.</p><p><b>Specified Duties: </b></p><p><b>Project Approval and Prioritization </b></p><p>•\tConsult with agency staff regarding the development of new projects.</p><p>•\tSupport the agency’s Project Management Portfolio process through analysis, presentations, and reports for the agency’s leadership.</p><p>•\tComplete the Planned Project Template for reportable projects.</p><p><b>Project Planning</b></p><p>Develop or assist in the development of project plans (including schedules, Communication Plans, Quality Plans, Deliverable Definition Documents, etc.), budget requests, and management procedures.</p><p>•\tInitiate project specific tools (such as MS Project and SharePoint) and practices within the State of Kansas guidelines which will be used to facilitate project tracking, reporting, and collaboration.</p><p>•\tCoordinate and develop High Level and Detailed planning documents for reportable projects.</p><p>•\tCoordinate and develop Federal Planning and Implementation Advanced Planning Documents (APD). </p><p>•\tEvaluate project plans for compliance with architecture, standards, policies, and guidelines.</p><p>•\tProvide IT project oversight to agency stakeholders and leadership for compliance with information technology planning guidelines, standards, policies and methodologies.</p><p><b>Project Execution</b></p><p>•\tManage IT project plans and coordinate the work of project members, internal and contracted, working on the project.</p><p>•\tTrack project progress against established timeline, budget, and deliverable definitions.</p><p>•\tMaintain project specific tools and practices to ensure effective project tracking, reporting, and collaboration.</p><p>•\tIdentify, report, and facilitate the resolution of project deficiencies in the form of issues and risks.</p><p>•\tConsult with agency stakeholders and leadership on progress of projects.</p><p>•\tProvide project related presentations/briefings as required.</p><p>•\tCoordinate and provide reporting on reportable projects</p><p>•\tConduct lessons learned sessions and develop close out documentation.</p><p><b>General Duties</b></p><p>•\tProvide support for the Project Management Office’s overall responsibilities, such as, agency project portfolio management, liaison and reporting requirements, and maintenance of agency project management tools.</p><p>•\tAssist Project Analysts and other Project Managers as required. </p><p>•\tOther duties as assigned.</p><p><b>Education Required: </b></p><p>•\tHigh school diploma or GED</p><p><b>Preferred Qualifications:</b></p><p>•\tFour years of experience with IT-related project management</p><p>•\tMust possess a certification or a traditional IT Project Management Methodology, such as the Project Management Professional (PMP) certification from the Project Management Institute (PMI)</p>",
