    "description": "• The Certified Microsoft .NET Web Developer IV is responsible for day-to-day maintenance of applications and support for business requests. \n• The person in this role will manage integrations. This project requires knowledge of full stack development. This is an application support position.\n• Experience designing, developing, and implementing web-based applications using the .NET framework to support business requirements. Includes the use of related development technologies such as ASP.NET, MVC, .NET CORE, and supported programming languages (e.g., C#, C++, bootstrap) and scripting languages (e.g., TypeScript, JavaScript).\n• Performs front-end and back-end development of web applications and web APIs (web services).\n• Experience with ASP.net and SSRS reporting.\n• Follows approved life cycle methodologies, creates documentation, and performs application coding and testing. Resolves technical issues through debugging, research, and investigation.\n• Requires a bachelors or associate degree in area of specialty or 5-8+ years of experience in the field or a related area.\n• Excellent verbal and written communication and best use of judgment and diplomacy.\n• Implementing or using security controls directly into the software development lifecycle, including GitHub Advanced Security.\n• Experience with SQL Server and relational databases.\n• This position requires knowledge of secure software development frameworks, including NIST 800-218 SSDF and ISO 27034 to ensure the delivery of secure and compliant systems.\n• Experience ensuring enforcement and advancement of security and DevSecOps standards through secure development practices, vulnerability remediation prioritization, automated testing, performance monitoring, and compliance with organizational security frameworks.\n• Provide support for security including vulnerability remediation, participation in security initiatives, escalation support for cybersecurity incidents. Ensure regulatory compliance in systems.\n\nTop Skills:\n\n• Development and Support experience on web-based applications using the .NET framework ASP.NET, MVC, .NET CORE.\n• Supported programming languages (e.g., C#, C, bootstrap) and scripting languages (e.g., TypeScript, JavaScript).\n• Experience with ASP.net and SSRS reporting\n• SQL Backend and stored procedure experience\n• Performs front-end and back-end development of web applications and web APIs (web services).\nNice to Have:\n• Experience with Kendo UI Controls\n• Experience with Power BI",
