    "description": "• Configuration Analyst supports Client's provisioning, MFA enrollment, PATH NC access, troubleshooting, and reporting. Works with state and county admins via ServiceNow; requires strong analysis and clear communication skills.  \n• The primary purpose of the Configuration Analyst is to assist with provisioning and troubleshooting user accounts/issues associated with the Client in production and training environments for PATH NC. \n• This position will assist users with understanding multifaction authentication (MFA) and assist with confirming each user has successfully enrolled in MFA. \n• This position works closely with state and county systems administrators via the Service Now (SNOW) ticketing system. \n• In addition, this position will assist with granting access to users so they can export reports from PATH NC. \n• Skills Ability to research, analyze and interpret automated system issues \n• Ability to communicate clearly and concisely in oral and written form with staff at all levels using excellent telephone etiquette and skills.\n\nSkills Required:\n\n• Experience and knowledge of browser-based applications.\tRequired\t3\tYears\n• Experience researching, analyzing and interpreting automated system problems.\tRequired\t5\tYears\n• Experience working in an Application Support-based (not hardware) help desk environment.\tRequired\t1\tYears\n• Broad knowledge of the PATH NC application and functionality.\tDesired\t1\tYears\n• Experience working with Identify Management and MultiFactor Authentication (MFA).\tDesired\t1\tYears",
    "rawDescription": "<p></p><ul><li>Configuration Analyst supports Client's provisioning, MFA enrollment, PATH NC access, troubleshooting, and reporting. Works with state and county admins via ServiceNow; requires strong analysis and clear communication skills.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>The primary purpose of the Configuration Analyst is to assist with provisioning and troubleshooting user accounts/issues associated with the Client in production and training environments for PATH NC.&nbsp;</li><li>This position will assist users with understanding multifaction authentication (MFA) and assist with confirming each user has successfully enrolled in MFA.&nbsp;</li><li>This position works closely with state and county systems administrators via the Service Now (SNOW) ticketing system.&nbsp;</li><li>In addition, this position will assist with granting access to users so they can export reports from PATH NC.&nbsp;</li><li>Skills Ability to research, analyze and interpret automated system issues&nbsp;</li><li>Ability to communicate clearly and concisely in oral and written form with staff at all levels using excellent telephone etiquette and skills.</li></ul><p></p><p><b>Skills Required:</b></p><p></p><ul><li>Experience and knowledge of browser-based applications.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Required<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>3<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Years</li><li>Experience researching, analyzing and interpreting automated system problems.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Required<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>5<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Years</li><li>Experience working in an Application Support-based (not hardware) help desk environment.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Required<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>1<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Years</li><li>Broad knowledge of the PATH NC application and functionality.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Desired<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>1<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Years</li><li>Experience working with Identify Management and MultiFactor Authentication (MFA).<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Desired<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>1<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Years</li></ul><p></p><p><br></p><p></p>",
    "htmlDescription": "<p></p><ul><li>Configuration Analyst supports Client's provisioning, MFA enrollment, PATH NC access, troubleshooting, and reporting. Works with state and county admins via ServiceNow; requires strong analysis and clear communication skills.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>The primary purpose of the Configuration Analyst is to assist with provisioning and troubleshooting user accounts/issues associated with the Client in production and training environments for PATH NC.&nbsp;</li><li>This position will assist users with understanding multifaction authentication (MFA) and assist with confirming each user has successfully enrolled in MFA.&nbsp;</li><li>This position works closely with state and county systems administrators via the Service Now (SNOW) ticketing system.&nbsp;</li><li>In addition, this position will assist with granting access to users so they can export reports from PATH NC.&nbsp;</li><li>Skills Ability to research, analyze and interpret automated system issues&nbsp;</li><li>Ability to communicate clearly and concisely in oral and written form with staff at all levels using excellent telephone etiquette and skills.</li></ul><p></p><p><b>Skills Required:</b></p><p></p><ul><li>Experience and knowledge of browser-based applications.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Required<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>3<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Years</li><li>Experience researching, analyzing and interpreting automated system problems.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Required<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>5<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Years</li><li>Experience working in an Application Support-based (not hardware) help desk environment.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Required<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>1<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Years</li><li>Broad knowledge of the PATH NC application and functionality.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Desired<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>1<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Years</li><li>Experience working with Identify Management and MultiFactor Authentication (MFA).<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Desired<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>1<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Years</li></ul><p></p><p><br></p><p></p>",
