    "description": "The Client is seeking qualified and passionate individuals for the role of Training & Coaching Officer. This position is responsible for delivering comprehensive Pre-Service and Specialty training to newly hired DCS staff as well as serving as an information liaison for new-hires during onboarding & throughout Pre-Service. The ideal candidate will have direct child welfare experience and a strong background in training delivery, with a commitment to trauma-informed care and the client's Practice Model.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n• Deliver Pre-Service Training to client's new employees, covering:\n• Fundamentals of Child Welfare\n• Program-specific content based on assigned service areas (e.g., CPS, Foster Care, Juvenile Justice)\n• Trauma-informed case management practices\n• The client's Practice Model and Practice Wheel (Engagement, Teaming,\n• Assessment, Planning, Implementation, Tracking, and Adjusting)\n• Self-care strategies and Motivational Interviewing techniques\\\n• Provide Coaching & Feedback to new hires based on field observation & identified practice gaps.\n• Facilitate Mentor Certification Programs\n• Proctor Pre-Service Assessments and support evaluation processes\n• Participate in Case Panel Presentations\n• Participate in Simulation Lab activities (depending on location)\n• Provide web-based technical assistance and support for virtual training delivery\n• Utilize Microsoft Teams and other digital platforms to conduct and support training sessions\n• Collaborate with training team members, program leadership & regional leadership to ensure consistency and quality in training content and delivery\n• Travel –some travel will be required\n• Mileage reimbursement will be available\n\nMinimum Qualifications:\n\n• One (1) year of direct child welfare field experience (e.g., case management, investigations, foster care, juvenile justice)\n• One (1) year of experience in training delivery, adult education, or staff development\n• Proficiency in Microsoft Teams and other virtual training tools\n• Strong communication, facilitation, and organizational skills\n• Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced, evolving training environment\n• Bachelor's Degree\n\nPreferred Qualifications:\n\n• Experience delivering training in a government or human services setting\n• Certification or coursework in trauma-informed care, motivational interviewing, or adult learning principles\n• Microsoft Excel -Novice (1-3 Years)\n• Microsoft PowerPoint - Novice (1-3 Years)\n• Microsoft Word - Novice (1-3 Years)\n\nWork Conditions:\n\n• Travel will be required for in-person training & coaching sessions as well as field observations.",
