    "description": "• The UiPath Developer is responsible for designing, developing, testing, deploying, and maintaining Robotic Process Automation (RPA) solutions that improve operational efficiency, accuracy, compliance, and citizen service delivery across agencies. This role supports both traditional linear automation workflows and emerging Agentic AI solutions using UiPath’s automation platform.\n\nKey Duties and Responsibilities\n\n• Design, develop, test, and implement UiPath automation solutions for business processes.\n• Build and maintain automations including attended, unattended, and scheduled bots for repetitive, rules-based workflows.\n• Analyze business requirements and translate them into scalable automation solutions using UiPath Studio, UiPath Studio Web, Orchestrator, and related technologies.\n• Develop process workflows, exception handling, logging, auditing, and monitoring capabilities for enterprise-grade automation.\n• Create reusable automation components, libraries, & templates to support enterprise automation initiatives.\n• Support integration of UiPath solutions with government systems, databases, APIs, document management systems, and cloud services.\n• Implement secure automation practices aligned with cybersecurity, privacy, and compliance standards.\n• Perform testing, debugging, troubleshooting, and ongoing maintenance of automation solutions.\n• Monitor bot performance, resolve production issues, and optimize automation reliability and efficiency.\n• Develop technical documentation and workflow diagrams.\n• Support citizen service modernization initiatives through intelligent automation technologies.\n\nAgentic AI Responsibilities\n\n• Design and implement Agentic AI solutions using UiPath Autopilot, AI Center, Document Understanding, Communications Mining, and generative AI capabilities.\n• Develop AI-powered agents capable of autonomous decision-making, contextual reasoning, and multi-step task orchestration within defined governance controls.\n• Integrate Large Language Models (LLMs), AI services, and intelligent document processing into automation workflows.\n• Build human-in-the-loop workflows that combine AI agents with employee oversight and approval processes.\n• Develop intelligent agents capable of interpreting unstructured data, emails, forms, documents, and citizen communications.\n• Implement retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), prompt engineering, and AI orchestration techniques within UiPath ecosystems.\n• Ensure responsible AI practices including transparency, auditability, bias mitigation, security, and compliance with government policies.\n• Evaluate emerging AI and automation technologies to improve operational efficiency and service delivery.\n• Assist with establishing enterprise standards and governance for Agentic AI implementations across agencies.\n\nPreferred Technical Skills\n\n• UiPath Studio, StudioX, Orchestrator, AI Center, Action Center, and Document Understanding\n• REFramework and enterprise RPA design patterns\n• API integrations, REST/SOAP services, SQL databases\n• OCR technologies and intelligent document processing\n• Generative AI, LLM integration, prompt engineering, and AI orchestration\n• Programming/scripting languages such as C#, VB.NET, Python, PowerShell, or JavaScript\n• Cloud platforms and enterprise authentication/security concepts\n• Agile/Scrum development methodologies",
    "rawDescription": "<p></p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 8.5px; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family:\"></p><ul><li>The UiPath Developer is responsible for designing, developing, testing, deploying, and maintaining Robotic Process Automation (RPA) solutions that improve operational efficiency, accuracy, compliance, and citizen service delivery across agencies. This role supports both traditional linear automation workflows and emerging Agentic AI solutions using UiPath’s automation platform.</li></ul><p></p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 8.5px; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family:\"><b>Key Duties and Responsibilities</b><br></p><ul style=\"\"><li style=\"\">Design, develop, test, and implement UiPath automation solutions for business processes.</li><li style=\"\">Build and maintain automations including attended, unattended, and scheduled bots for repetitive, rules-based workflows.</li><li style=\"\">Analyze business requirements and translate them into scalable automation solutions using UiPath Studio, UiPath Studio Web, Orchestrator, and related technologies.</li><li style=\"\">Develop process workflows, exception handling, logging, auditing, and monitoring capabilities for enterprise-grade automation.</li><li style=\"\">Create reusable automation components, libraries, &amp; templates to support enterprise automation initiatives.</li><li style=\"\">Support integration of UiPath solutions with government systems, databases, APIs, document management systems, and cloud services.</li><li style=\"\">Implement secure automation practices aligned with cybersecurity, privacy, and compliance standards.</li><li style=\"\">Perform testing, debugging, troubleshooting, and ongoing maintenance of automation solutions.</li><li style=\"\">Monitor bot performance, resolve production issues, and optimize automation reliability and efficiency.</li><li style=\"\">Develop technical documentation and workflow diagrams.</li><li style=\"\">Support citizen service modernization initiatives through intelligent automation technologies.</li></ul><p></p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 8.5px; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family:\"><b>Agentic AI Responsibilities</b><br></p><ul style=\"\"><li style=\"\">Design and implement Agentic AI solutions using UiPath Autopilot, AI Center, Document Understanding, Communications Mining, and generative AI capabilities.</li><li style=\"\">Develop AI-powered agents capable of autonomous decision-making, contextual reasoning, and multi-step task orchestration within defined governance controls.</li><li style=\"\">Integrate Large Language Models (LLMs), AI services, and intelligent document processing into automation workflows.</li><li style=\"\">Build human-in-the-loop workflows that combine AI agents with employee oversight and approval processes.</li><li style=\"\">Develop intelligent agents capable of interpreting unstructured data, emails, forms, documents, and citizen communications.</li><li style=\"\">Implement retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), prompt engineering, and AI orchestration techniques within UiPath ecosystems.</li><li style=\"\">Ensure responsible AI practices including transparency, auditability, bias mitigation, security, and compliance with government policies.</li><li style=\"\">Evaluate emerging AI and automation technologies to improve operational efficiency and service delivery.</li><li style=\"\">Assist with establishing enterprise standards and governance for Agentic AI implementations across agencies.</li></ul><p></p><p style=\"margin: 0px 0px 8.5px; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family:\"><b>Preferred Technical Skills</b><br></p><ul style=\"\"><li style=\"\">UiPath Studio, StudioX, Orchestrator, AI Center, Action Center, and Document Understanding</li><li style=\"\">REFramework and enterprise RPA design patterns</li><li style=\"\">API integrations, REST/SOAP services, SQL databases</li><li style=\"\">OCR technologies and intelligent document processing</li><li style=\"\">Generative AI, LLM integration, prompt engineering, and AI orchestration</li><li style=\"\">Programming/scripting languages such as C#, VB.NET, Python, PowerShell, or JavaScript</li><li style=\"\">Cloud platforms and enterprise authentication/security concepts</li><li style=\"\">Agile/Scrum development methodologies</li></ul><p></p><p></p>",
