    "description": "Under general supervision, analyzes customer business needs and participates in the planning, design and implementation of new or enhanced systems.\n\nThe Senior Business Analyst for KOALA is responsible for analyzing business needs and supporting the planning, design, and implementation of new or enhanced systems for the client. This role serves as the primary subject matter expert for KOALA, providing guidance to Child Care  Services (CCS), Legal/CRC units, the client application development team, and third-party vendors. The position also supports KOALA production activities, enhancements, and testing. \n\nCore Responsibilities \n\n• Ensure KOALA application functionality, requirements, and industry standards are accurately defined and implemented. \n• Serve as the primary subject matter expert for KOALA program operations. \n• Coordinate KOALA maintenance and support activities, representing agency interests. \n• Develop detailed business requirements and system documentation. \n• Assist CCS with creating KOALA user training materials, including screenshots and guidance. \n• Develop and execute test plans; support user acceptance testing and data preparation. \n• Participate in KOALA enhancement projects through the full project lifecycle, from definition through evaluation. \n• Build collaborative partnerships with internal teams and external vendors to ensure timely and successful deliverables. \n• Fulfill data requests as needed. \nTechnical Skills & Competencies \n\n• Experience managing IT projects and writing business requirements. \n• Strong self-starter who can work independently. \n• Excellent written and verbal communication skills. \n• Ability to communicate effectively with CCS and Legal staff. \n• Strong command of English grammar, punctuation, and writing conventions. \n• Ability to quickly understand and translate stakeholder needs. \n• Receptive to direction, feedback, and editing. \n• Logical, analytical, and detail-oriented. \n• Proficiency with Microsoft Office, Balsamiq, Azure DevOps, and SQL scripting. \nPhysical Requirements \n\n• Ability to receive and understand information through oral communication. \n• Clear, effective verbal communication. \n• Ability to hear and understand normal conversation levels. \n• Close visual acuity for data analysis, transcription, computer work, reading, and visual inspection. \n• Ability to review, categorize, prioritize, and analyze data using discretion and judgment. \n• Ability to apply evaluative reasoning in situations requiring subjective analysis. \nPreferred Qualifications \n\n• Bachelor’s degree in a related field with 10+ years of relevant experience.",
    "rawDescription": "<p>Under general supervision, analyzes customer business needs and participates in the planning, design and implementation of new or enhanced systems.</p><p>The Senior Business Analyst for KOALA is responsible for analyzing business needs and supporting the planning, design, and implementation of new or enhanced systems for the client. This role serves as the primary subject matter expert for KOALA, providing guidance to Child Care&nbsp; Services (CCS), Legal/CRC units, the client application development team, and third-party vendors. The position also supports KOALA production activities, enhancements, and testing.&nbsp;</p><p><b>Core Responsibilities&nbsp;</b></p><ul><li>Ensure KOALA application functionality, requirements, and industry standards are accurately defined and implemented.&nbsp;</li><li>Serve as the primary subject matter expert for KOALA program operations.&nbsp;</li><li>Coordinate KOALA maintenance and support activities, representing agency interests.&nbsp;</li><li>Develop detailed business requirements and system documentation.&nbsp;</li><li>Assist CCS with creating KOALA user training materials, including screenshots and guidance.&nbsp;</li><li>Develop and execute test plans; support user acceptance testing and data preparation.&nbsp;</li><li>Participate in KOALA enhancement projects through the full project lifecycle, from definition through evaluation.&nbsp;</li><li>Build collaborative partnerships with internal teams and external vendors to ensure timely and successful deliverables.&nbsp;</li><li>Fulfill data requests as needed.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><b>Technical Skills &amp; Competencies&nbsp;</b></p><ul><li>Experience managing IT projects and writing business requirements.&nbsp;</li><li>Strong self-starter who can work independently.&nbsp;</li><li>Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&nbsp;</li><li>Ability to communicate effectively with CCS and Legal staff.&nbsp;</li><li>Strong command of English grammar, punctuation, and writing conventions.&nbsp;</li><li>Ability to quickly understand and translate stakeholder needs.&nbsp;</li><li>Receptive to direction, feedback, and editing.&nbsp;</li><li>Logical, analytical, and detail-oriented.&nbsp;</li><li>Proficiency with Microsoft Office, Balsamiq, Azure DevOps, and SQL scripting.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><b>Physical Requirements&nbsp;</b></p><ul><li>Ability to receive and understand information through oral communication.&nbsp;</li><li>Clear, effective verbal communication.&nbsp;</li><li>Ability to hear and understand normal conversation levels.&nbsp;</li><li>Close visual acuity for data analysis, transcription, computer work, reading, and visual inspection.&nbsp;</li><li>Ability to review, categorize, prioritize, and analyze data using discretion and judgment.&nbsp;</li><li>Ability to apply evaluative reasoning in situations requiring subjective analysis.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><b>Preferred Qualifications&nbsp;</b></p><ul><li>Bachelor’s degree in a related field with 10+ years of relevant experience.</li></ul>",
