    "description": "• Providing primary application support for CityWorks which is being used by a select group of general government departments.\n• Performing application testing (test plans/cases and execution) and troubleshooting for all CityWorks and related systems and applications.\n• Performing business analysis activities for enterprise-wide application such as: work plan input, deliverable definition and tracking, status reporting, conducting user level meetings.\n• Report or form creation/modification in Crystal Reports and SQL queries using Cityworks and Land Management data.\n• Performing project analysis activities for enterprise-wide application projects such as: work plan input, deliverable definition and tracking, status reporting, conducting user level meetings, and preparing application requirements/specifications. \n• Coordinating and communicating with other team members including process owners, users, departments, ITS technical team, and consultants.\n• Data extracts from SQL based on user request and/or public request\n• Experience with CityWorks configuration and support, Crystal reporting, and SQL queries\n• Experience with SQL Server Management Studio (SSMS)\n• Experience writing SQL queries to update or extract data from a SQL database\n• Experience as systems analyst, supporting users with issues resolution, system enhancement, upgrades and conversion.\n• Experience coordinating and conducting end-user training including preparing and updating training materials.  As part of an implementation training rollout a plus.\n• Experience with Microsoft Office Suite.",
