    "description": "• The Budget Unit processes a high and growing volume of journal vouchers, contract authorizations, and budget revisions across state and federal funding sources.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n•  Prepare, review, and process journal vouchers so that expenditures and corrections are recorded accurately across the appropriate funding sources.\n•  Monitor contract spend against authorized budgets and produce regular reports on contract utilization, variances, and projected spend.\n•  Track fund utilization across state and federal sources and confirm that spending remains aligned with appropriated and certified amounts.\n•  Prepare and process budget revisions to the appropriation and certified budget, with clear documentation and an audit trail for each revision.\n•  Support reconciliation and respond to questions from program and finance staff on contract and budget matters\n\nSkills Required:\n\n•  Strong attention to detail and the ability to manage a high volume of transactions accurately.\n•  Proficiency with spreadsheets and financial systems, with the ability to produce clear reports for leadership.\n•  Ability to work independently and meet recurring deadlines.\n• Experience in budget analysis, accounting, or financial reporting, preferably in a government or healthcare finance setting.\tRequired\t3\tYears\n• Experience executing against multiple priorities/projects.\tRequired\t3\tYears\n• Proficient use of project collaboration and tracking tools (Microsoft Project Suite, MS Teams, Zoom, etc.)\tRequired\t3\tYears\n• Exceptional written and oral communication skills.\tRequired\t3\tYears\n• Experience monitoring Contract Spend on multiple Contracts\tRequired\t3\tYears\n• Prior state government/public sector experience with health and human services programs (such as Medicaid, Medicaid Management Information System (MMI\tHighly desired\t3\tYears\n• Experience with tracking fund utilization across state and federal sources\tRequired\t3\tYears",
    "rawDescription": "<p></p><ul><li>The Budget Unit processes a high and growing volume of journal vouchers, contract authorizations, and budget revisions across state and federal funding sources.</li></ul><p></p><p></p><p></p><p><b>Key Responsibilities</b></p><p></p><ul><li>&nbsp;Prepare, review, and process journal vouchers so that expenditures and corrections are recorded accurately across the appropriate funding sources.</li><li>&nbsp;Monitor contract spend against authorized budgets and produce regular reports on contract utilization, variances, and projected spend.</li><li>&nbsp;Track fund utilization across state and federal sources and confirm that spending remains aligned with appropriated and certified amounts.</li><li>&nbsp;Prepare and process budget revisions to the appropriation and certified budget, with clear documentation and an audit trail for each revision.</li><li>&nbsp;Support reconciliation and respond to questions from program and finance staff on contract and budget matters</li></ul><p></p><p></p><p></p><p><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">Skills Required:</span></p><p></p><p></p><ul><li>&nbsp;Strong attention to detail and the ability to manage a high volume of transactions accurately.</li><li>&nbsp;Proficiency with spreadsheets and financial systems, with the ability to produce clear reports for leadership.</li><li>&nbsp;Ability to work independently and meet recurring deadlines.</li><li>Experience in budget analysis, accounting, or financial reporting, preferably in a government or healthcare finance setting.<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">\t</span>Required<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">\t</span>3<span style=\"white-space: pre;\">\t</span>Years</li><li>Experience executing against multiple priorities/projects.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Required<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>3<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Years</li><li>Proficient use of project collaboration and tracking tools (Microsoft Project Suite, MS Teams, Zoom, etc.)<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Required<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>3<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Years</li><li>Exceptional written and oral communication skills.<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Required<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>3<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Years</li><li>Experience monitoring Contract Spend on multiple Contracts<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Required<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>3<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Years</li><li>Prior state government/public sector experience with health and human services programs (such as Medicaid, Medicaid Management Information System (MMI<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Highly desired<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>3<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Years</li><li>Experience with tracking fund utilization across state and federal sources<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Required<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>3<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Years</li></ul><p></p><p></p>",
