    "description": "• The position supports the Client as the Procurement Project Manager for the entire agency.  The position will serve as the technical liaison between Client and the Central Procurement Office (CPO) assisting in the development of proposals for bids while maintaining the interests of the  Procurement policies and procedures. This position will administer procurement activities from development and implementation of the sourcing strategy through award of the contract, which includes identifying agency needs, drafting solicitations, aid CPO in executing procurements and aid CPO in the evaluation. The position requires strong organizational skills and the ability to work with multiple schedules. This position requires excellent project and time management capabilities.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n• Develops and assists divisions in solicitation specifications based on internal and external sources of information\n• Possesses and demonstrates strong knowledge of policies, procedures and execution strategy for multiple solicitation methods including Request for Proposal, Request for Qualification, and Request for Information.\n• Regularly represents the client and the division of Grants and Contracts while speaking with internal and external stakeholders\n• Provides strategic advice and consultation to agency procurement and program staff to determine the proper methods of procurement as well as strategy development and execution of procurement activities\n\nQualifications\n\n• Graduation from an accredited college or university with a bachelor’s degree and 5 to 10 years of business, procurement, and/or contract management experience",
