    "description": "About the Role\n\nThis role is a client-facing leadership position responsible for managing end-to-end project delivery while also acting as a Scrum Master for multiple Agile teams. The individual will be accountable for ensuring projects are delivered on time, within budget, and according to customer expectations.Key Responsibilities:\n\n• Drive end-to-end project management activities ensuring successful delivery within scope, timeline, and budget\n• Owning the delivery end to end by exhibiting problem-solving skills\n• Lead Agile ceremonies and act as Scrum Master for multiple cross-functional teams at the same time\n• Owning the comprehensive Change management process at the customer side\n• At the customer side, preparing & Managing project plans, sprint backlogs, and workflows\n• Proactively suggesting improvements in the process and coming up with hard ($) savings/ soft savings (process improvements)\n• Responding quickly to the customer ask\n• Collaborate with Product Owners, Business Analysts, and stakeholders to define priorities and align project goals\n• Lead and mentor Project Management and Scrum teams\n• Provide regular project status updates, identify risks, and drive mitigation plans\n• Build strong client relationships through effective communication and stakeholder management\nRequired Skills:\n\n• Project Management experience along with hands-on Scrum Master experience\n• Strong expertise in JIRA and Monday.com (preferably at the admin level too)\n• Experience in managing large teams (including 3rd party vendors) and leading PM/SM functions\n• Scrum certified (CSM/PSM)\n• Must have handled US/UK customers\n• Confident personality with exceptional verbal and written communication skills\n• Excellent stakeholder management and client-facing communication skills\n• Experience working directly with Product Owners and Business Analysts\n• Ability to work with US stakeholders in overlapping time zones",
    "rawDescription": "<p><b><font size=\"3\">About the Role</font></b></p><div style=\"white-space: normal; font-family:\"><font size=\"3\">This role is a client-facing leadership position responsible for managing end-to-end project delivery while also acting as a Scrum Master for multiple Agile teams. The individual will be accountable for ensuring projects are delivered on time, within budget, and according to customer expectations.</font></div><p style=\"margin-left: 0px\"><strong><font size=\"3\">Key Responsibilities:</font></strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">Drive end-to-end project management activities ensuring successful delivery within scope, timeline, and budget</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\"><strong>Owning</strong> the delivery end to end by exhibiting problem-solving skills</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">Lead Agile ceremonies and act as Scrum Master for <strong>multiple</strong> cross-functional teams at the same time</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">Owning the comprehensive Change management process at the customer side</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">At the customer side, preparing &amp; Managing project plans, sprint backlogs, and workflows</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">Proactively suggesting improvements in the process and coming up with hard ($) savings/ soft savings (process improvements)</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">Responding quickly to the customer ask</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">Collaborate with Product Owners, Business Analysts, and stakeholders to define priorities and align project goals</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">Lead and mentor Project Management and Scrum teams</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">Provide regular project status updates, identify risks, and drive mitigation plans</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">Build strong client relationships through effective communication and stakeholder management</span></li></ul><p style=\"margin-left: 0px\"><span style=\"font-size: inherit\"><strong>Required Skills:</strong></span></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">Project Management experience along with hands-on Scrum Master experience</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">Strong expertise in JIRA and Monday.com (preferably at the admin level too)</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">Experience in managing large teams (including 3<i>rd</i> party vendors) and leading PM/SM functions</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">Scrum certified (CSM/PSM)</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">Must have handled US/UK customers</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">Confident personality with exceptional verbal and written communication skills</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">Excellent stakeholder management and client-facing communication skills</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">Experience working directly with Product Owners and Business Analysts</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: inherit\">Ability to work with US stakeholders in overlapping time zones</span></li></ul>",
