    "description": "We are looking for a detail-oriented and proactive QA Engineer with 2–5 years of experience in Manual and Automation Testing. The ideal candidate should possess strong testing fundamentals, hands-on experience in API and performance testing, and exposure to modern automation frameworks such as Playwright. The candidate should be capable of analyzing application logs, identifying issues, and ensuring high-quality software releases.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n• Design, develop, and execute test plans, test cases, and test scripts for web-based applications.\n• Perform comprehensive Manual Testing to validate application functionality and user experience.\n• Develop and maintain Automation Test Scripts using Playwright.\n• Conduct API Testing using tools such as Postman or similar platforms.\n• Execute Performance Testing and analyze application behavior under load.\n• Monitor, read, and analyze application and server logs to identify defects and troubleshoot issues.\n• Track, document, and manage defects through their complete lifecycle.\n• Collaborate closely with developers, Business Analysts, and stakeholders to ensure quality deliverables.\n• Participate in requirement analysis, sprint planning, and testing activities throughout the Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC).\n• Work with bug tracking and project management tools such as JIRA, Monday.com, or similar platforms.\n• Support infrastructure validation and environment verification activities when required.\nRequired Skills\n\n• 2–5 years of experience in Software Testing.\n• Strong understanding of SQL and Database concepts.\n• Hands-on experience in API Testing.\n• Experience in Manual and Automation Testing.\n• Practical knowledge of Playwright Automation Framework.\n• Experience in Performance Testing.\n• Ability to read, understand, and analyze application logs.\n• Good understanding of the Bug Lifecycle and defect management processes.\n• Basic understanding of SDLC and Agile methodologies.\n• Good verbal and written communication skills.\nGood-to-Have Skills\n\n• Experience with TOSCA and Selenium.\n• Exposure to Infrastructure Validation activities.\n• Knowledge of CI/CD pipelines and test automation best practices.\nPreferred Candidate Profile\n\n• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.\n• Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively within a team.\n• Quick learner with an eagerness to adopt new tools and technologies.",
    "rawDescription": "<p>We are looking for a detail-oriented and proactive QA Engineer with 2–5 years of experience in Manual and Automation Testing. The ideal candidate should possess strong testing fundamentals, hands-on experience in API and performance testing, and exposure to modern automation frameworks such as Playwright. The candidate should be capable of analyzing application logs, identifying issues, and ensuring high-quality software releases.</p><p>Key Responsibilities</p><ul><li>Design, develop, and execute test plans, test cases, and test scripts for web-based applications.</li><li>Perform comprehensive Manual Testing to validate application functionality and user experience.</li><li>Develop and maintain Automation Test Scripts using <strong>Playwright</strong>.</li><li>Conduct <strong>API Testing</strong> using tools such as Postman or similar platforms.</li><li>Execute <strong>Performance Testing</strong> and analyze application behavior under load.</li><li>Monitor, read, and analyze application and server logs to identify defects and troubleshoot issues.</li><li>Track, document, and manage defects through their complete lifecycle.</li><li>Collaborate closely with developers, Business Analysts, and stakeholders to ensure quality deliverables.</li><li>Participate in requirement analysis, sprint planning, and testing activities throughout the <strong>Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC)</strong>.</li><li>Work with bug tracking and project management tools such as <strong>JIRA, Monday.com, or similar platforms</strong>.</li><li>Support infrastructure validation and environment verification activities when required.</li></ul><p>Required Skills</p><ul><li>2–5 years of experience in Software Testing.</li><li>Strong understanding of <strong>SQL and Database concepts</strong>.</li><li>Hands-on experience in <strong>API Testing</strong>.</li><li>Experience in <strong>Manual and Automation Testing</strong>.</li><li>Practical knowledge of <strong>Playwright Automation Framework</strong>.</li><li>Experience in <strong>Performance Testing</strong>.</li><li>Ability to read, understand, and analyze application logs.</li><li>Good understanding of the <strong>Bug Lifecycle</strong> and defect management processes.</li><li>Basic understanding of <strong>SDLC and Agile methodologies</strong>.</li><li>Good verbal and written communication skills.</li></ul><p>Good-to-Have Skills</p><ul><li>Experience with <strong>TOSCA</strong> and <strong>Selenium</strong>.</li><li>Exposure to <strong>Infrastructure Validation</strong> activities.</li><li>Knowledge of CI/CD pipelines and test automation best practices.</li></ul><p>Preferred Candidate Profile</p><ul><li>Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.</li><li>Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively within a team.</li><li>Quick learner with an eagerness to adopt new tools and technologies.</li></ul>",
