    "description": "Technical Skills Required\n\nMinimum 10+ years in infrastructure / solution architecture with expertise in designing, deploying, and managing enterprise-scale EUC and Digital Workspace solutions\n\nStrong expertise in Virtualization technologies, Windows, and Linux OS\n\nProficiency in Networking, Storage, Active Directory (AD), DNS, File Servers, and Security solutions\n\nHands-on experience in designing solutions for Virtual Desktop Infrastructure (VDI) and Application Virtualization\n\nHands-on experience in sizing large-scale environments\n\nExperience handling and managing Large Scale, Enterprise, and Strategic customers\n\nAdvanced troubleshooting skills across Windows and Linux environments\n\nProven client engagement and account management capabilities\n\nStrategic mindset with the ability to mentor, inspire, and drive organizational learning\n\nRoles and Responsibilities\n\nArchitect, design, and implement End-User Computing (EUC) solutions that are secure, scalable, and aligned with evolving client and market needs\n\nPartner with Engineering teams to co-develop new features and ensure alignment of infrastructure initiatives with product roadmaps\n\nCollaborate with Presales teams to design and deliver technical bootcamps, empowering teams with future-ready skills\n\nContribute to creation of blogs, white papers, validated designs, design templates, and architecture templates\n\nCollaborate with the L&D function for trainings\n\nAct as a trusted advisor and technology leader within the Customer Success function, helping in upskilling Professional Services and Technical Support teams\n\nProvide Quality Assurance for documentation created by the Professional Services and Pre-Sales teams\n\nRepresent the organization as a Technology Leader in front of customers\n\nGood to Have Skills\n\nExperience in Identity & Access Management (IAM)\n\nExposure to Cybersecurity products\n\nExperience with ZTNA (Zero Trust Network Access)\n\nExposure to DevOps practices\n\nExperience in Infrastructure Automation\n\nFamiliarity with Monitoring tools\n\nSoft Skills Required\n\nCross-functional leadership\n\nTechnical enablement & partner programs\n\nStrategic account management\n\nTeam development & mentoring\n\nInfrastructure design & optimization\n\nProactive problem-solving and continuous improvement",
